{
  "info": {
    "name": "Message Broker Service",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "The Message Broker 4.0.0 (Lab 4), its HTTP side on port 8070: the probes, the topics and dead letter listings (X-Service-Token), GET /logs (#112) and GET /metrics (#126). docs/MESSAGE_BROKER.md is the reference. On a new broker both listings are empty. Set base_url and service_token (the placeholder of .env.example) for your stack.\n\nThe gRPC API on port 8071 (Publish, Subscribe, Ack, Request, Reply, ListTopics, ListDeadLetters) is not in this collection, which holds HTTP requests only. It is called with scripts/smoke.py from the root of the broker's repository, with SERVICE_TOKEN in the environment and --broker host:port (default 127.0.0.1:8071):\n\n  python -m scripts.smoke subscribe --service player --instance player-1 --topic events.session.ended\n  python -m scripts.smoke publish --topic events.session.ended --event-id e1\n  python -m scripts.smoke topics\n  python -m scripts.smoke request --service player --method GET --path /api/v1/players\n\nTo fill the dead letter listing, run the subscriber alone with --outcome permanent and publish again."
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "base_url", "value": "http://localhost:8070" },
    { "key": "service_token", "value": "change_me_too" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "probes",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /health",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('names the broker', () => pm.expect(b.service).to.eql('message-broker'));",
                  "pm.test('a Lab 4 version', () => pm.expect(b.version).to.match(/^4\\.\\d+\\.\\d+$/));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": { "method": "GET", "header": [], "url": "{{base_url}}/health" }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /status",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('contract shape and the gRPC threads', () => pm.expect(b).to.have.all.keys('service','instance_id','version','status','in_flight','max_concurrent_tasks','grpc_in_flight','grpc_max_workers'));",
                  "pm.test('names the broker', () => pm.expect(b.service).to.eql('message-broker'));",
                  "pm.test('up, the store writes', () => pm.expect(b.status).to.eql('up'));",
                  "pm.test('gRPC threads within the pool', () => pm.expect(b.grpc_in_flight).to.be.within(0, b.grpc_max_workers));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": { "method": "GET", "header": [], "url": "{{base_url}}/status" }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /metrics",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('the Prometheus text format', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.include('text/plain'));",
                  "const body = pm.response.text();",
                  "pm.test('the shared series', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.include('# TYPE http_requests_total counter');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.include('tasks_in_flight');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('the broker series', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.include('broker_queue_depth');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.include('broker_redeliveries_total');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.include('broker_dead_letters_total');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": { "method": "GET", "header": [], "url": "{{base_url}}/metrics" }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /api/v1/nope - an unknown path is 404",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('404', () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));",
                  "pm.test('NOT_FOUND', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error.code).to.eql('NOT_FOUND'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/nope",
            "description": "Answered in the shared error envelope, before the service token is looked at."
          }
        }
